{
  "_notes": [
    "Hand-authored modern encounter tables, consumed by tools/generate_gen9_authored.py -> lib/gen9_encounters_authored.lua.",
    "",
    "1) PRIMARY tables (Gen 3-9, dex 252..1025) for the Gen 1 areas the generated Essentials data does not cover:",
    "   Route 18, Route 24, Victory Road 1F/2F/3F and the Super Rod groups of Cerulean Gym, Route 11, Route 24, Safari Zone",
    "   East and Vermilion Dock.",
    "2) `classic` tables (Gen 2, dex 152..251): the fill used when the MAX GEN cap leaves the primary table with NO slot",
    "   (a Gen 2 cap drops every Gen 3-9 species). Without them those areas fall back to the original game's table. They cover",
    "   the 10 areas above plus the 12 generated tables that hold no Gen 1-2 species at all (Route 17 and 23 grass, Route 20/21",
    "   water, the Super Rods of Cerulean Cave 1F/2F/B1F, Route 20, 21, 23, 25 and Safari Zone North).",
    "",
    "Each grass/water row is { species, min, max, pct }: the row's pct is spread evenly over min..max (same quantization as",
    "tools/generate_gen9_encounters.py). Levels here only need to be plausible: at runtime lib/gen9_encounters.lua re-anchors them",
    "onto the original game's level distribution for the same map, ranking species by these levels and then by base-stat total.",
    "Super Rod entries are { species, level }; a group keeps the ORIGINAL group's size, because the engine's bite chance depends on it.",
    "",
    "`bands` is what keeps every pick in the realm of its part of the game. The generator refuses a species outside the band:",
    "  bst    inclusive base-stat total (hp+atk+def+spe+spa+spd) around the ORIGINAL area's own species",
    "  stages allowed evolution positions: single | base | mid | final (position in its chain)",
    "  types  optional: the species must have at least one of these types",
    "Species must be in the table's generation range and not legendary/mythical/Ultra Beast/Paradox (lib/species_flags_data.lua)."
  ],
